# Interva

A modern, open-source Pomodoro timer built for students and developers who need a clean, distraction-free focus tool.

## What It Does

Interva is a desktop Pomodoro timer application that helps you stay focused with customizable work/break intervals. Built with Tauri for a lightweight native experience, it's available on Windows, macOS, and Linux.

## Technical Highlights

- **Desktop Framework**: Tauri (Rust backend) keeps the app lightweight — no bloated Electron runtime
- **Frontend**: React + TypeScript + Tailwind + DaisyUI for a polished, responsive UI
- **35+ Themes**: Fully customizable color schemes with smooth transitions
- **CI/CD Pipeline**: GitHub Actions automatically builds `.msi`, `.dmg`, and `.AppImage` on every version tag
- **Landing Page**: Next.js + ShadCN + Vercel for the marketing site

## What I Learned

This was my first real dive into desktop app distribution. Dealing with unsigned binaries, Windows Defender false positives, and macOS Gatekeeper was a crash course in the realities of shipping software to real users. Setting up automated cross-platform builds with GitHub Actions taught me CI/CD fundamentals that I now use on every project.

